```java
public void clear() {
    circularClear(elements, head, tail);
    head = tail = 0;
    // @@@ the deque is empty after this operation
}
```

We need to write an assert statement that captures that after clear(), the deque is empty. There is a public method isEmpty() that returns true if deque contains no elements. Also size() returns number of elements. We can use either isEmpty() or size()==0. Use public observer methods: isEmpty() or size(). So assertion: assert this.isEmpty(); or assert this.size() == 0; Both are fine. Use isEmpty().

